# GoClaw — Go Conventions

## Language Rule — STRICT
**All code, comments, identifiers, error messages, and log strings must be in English.**

**Agent-authored Markdown** at the repo root — `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, `.cursor/skills/**/*.md`, `.claude/skills/*.md` — must also be **English only** (headings, body, examples, frontmatter `description:`). See `.cursor/rules/agent-artifacts-english.mdc`.

```go
// CORRECT
// Execute runs the tool with the given JSON input.
func (t *ReadFileTool) Execute(ctx context.Context, input string) (Result, error)

// WRONG — non-English comment
// Ejecuta el tool con el input JSON dado.
```

## Logging
```go
// CORRECT
slog.Info("tool executed", "name", toolName, "duration", elapsed)
slog.Error("llm stream failed", "err", err)

// FORBIDDEN
fmt.Println("tool executed:", toolName)
log.Printf("error: %v", err)
```

## Error Handling
```go
// Wrap with context — always
return fmt.Errorf("read_file: open %s: %w", path, err)

// Error strings: lowercase, no trailing punctuation
errors.New("permission denied")          // CORRECT
errors.New("Permission denied.")         // WRONG

// Match errors structurally
if errors.Is(err, ErrPermissionDenied) { ... }   // CORRECT
if err == ErrPermissionDenied { ... }            // WRONG

// Sentinel errors at package level
var ErrPermissionDenied = errors.New("permission denied")
```

## Interfaces
```go
// CORRECT — base name or -er suffix, small (1–3 methods)
type Client interface { Stream(...) }
type Tool interface { Execute(...) }

// FORBIDDEN
type IClient interface{}
type ToolInterface interface{}

// Compile-time interface satisfaction check
var _ Tool = (*ReadFileTool)(nil)
```

## Context
```go
// CORRECT — first parameter always
func (t *ReadFileTool) Execute(ctx context.Context, input string) (Result, error)

// FORBIDDEN
func (t *ReadFileTool) Execute(input string) (Result, error)
```

## Defer
```go
resp, err := http.Get(url)
if err != nil { return err }
defer resp.Body.Close()  // immediately after acquisition
```

## Concurrency
```go
// Channel direction in signatures — always explicit
func produce(out chan<- Event) { ... }
func consume(in <-chan Event)  { ... }

// Always provide a goroutine exit path
go func() {
    defer close(out)
    select {
    case out <- event:
    case <-ctx.Done():
        return
    }
}()
```

## Dependency Injection
```go
// CORRECT — inject all dependencies
func New(cfg Config, client llm.Client) *Orchestrator

// FORBIDDEN — hidden global
var globalClient llm.Client
```

## Naming
- Tool names exposed to the model: `snake_case` (read_file, web_fetch)
- Internal Go types: `CamelCase` (ReadFileTool, AnthropicClient)

### Full words — no lazy abbreviations
No lazy truncations (`fun`, `re`, generic `str`, vague `cnt`/`tmp`, …). Use domain-clear names at call sites. Idiomatic Go shorts stay OK (`ctx`, `err`, `ok`, `i`/`j`, `t`/`tb`, HTTP `r`/`w`, `mu`, tight-scope `buf`). Details: `.cursor/rules/naming-full-words.mdc` and `.claude/skills/naming-full-words.md`.

## Forbidden
- `fmt.Println` for logging
- `panic()` except for unrecoverable programming errors
- `init()` functions
- Mutable global variables without `sync.Once`
- Ignoring errors with `_`
- `log.Fatal` / `log.Panic`
- Returning concrete types when an interface suffices
- Non-English text anywhere in code
